Taking a random YouTube video, the kind filmed just for fun, and throwing it at our systems to see what happens.

This time: footage from a DJI FPV Drone with a GoPro Hero 8 mounted on top, flying through Fjaðrárgljúfur canyon in Iceland. A steep-walled gorge carved by glacial meltwater. Stunning scenery, and a challenging sequence for any VSLAM system.

Starting from a single YAML file, I ran it through three VSLAM systems: MASt3R-SLAM, DROID-SLAM and AllFeature-VSLAM — our system, tightly coupling ORB + SuperPoint features. And compare the estimated trajectories with the one estimated from SfM GLOMAP

Every experiment is fully reproducible with a single command:

pixi run vslamlab configs/test_exp_youtube.yaml --overwrite

Real-world, uncontrolled footage, no lab setup, no carefully curated benchmark, just a drone flying through a canyon and algorithms trying to make sense of it all.

